  "reason": "Evidence: config_033 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) is the best result so far at 0.7131 acc / 0.6945 F1, and the pattern across configs 030→031→033 shows that transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the strongest combination. However, the image-only resnet50 baseline (config_010) is very weak (0.2079), raising uncertainty about whether the image modality is contributing meaningfully or whether a stronger image encoder is needed. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l improve the best-performing multimodal configuration? This is a single-variable change (image encoder only) from config_033, cleanly isolating the effect of image representation quality. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly exploits the strongest evidence (best config) along the one untested dimension, and the answer has high downstream value—if ViT-L helps substantially, it confirms image features are a bottleneck and justifies further image-encoder exploration; if it does not, it confirms the current configuration is near its ceiling and redirects budget toward other axes (e.g., RNA-only transformer via config_006 or fusion ablation via config_032)."
}

